  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday night through next Tuesday)\nIssued at 1236 PM CST Wed Nov 25 2026\n\nUpper flow will remain out of the northwest through Friday before a \nprogressive upper shortwave trough pushes southeastward from the \nPacific Northwest. This system will be dry with no precip expected, \nbut it will push a cold front through the FA by Saturday evening and \nwill bring near to above advisory level winds. This will bring \nafternoon highs down from near 70 on Saturday to the mid 40s/50s \nSunday. The cool-down will be short lived as there will be a return \nto surface lee troughing across the Plains with winds veering to the \nsouth to southwest Monday.",
